# Pages generated by tools/build.mjs from content/articles/*.json (Nexus One articles) are build output and are NOT committed, but they cannot be
# ignored by a path pattern: hand-written articles live in the same folders (public/clanky/<slug>/index.html) and must stay trackable.
# Instead, tests/articles.test.js fails when a tracked page carries <meta name="nexus-article"> (generated). After a local build do not
# `git add -A` public/clanky/ or public/sitemap.xml: `git restore public/clanky/index.html public/sitemap.xml` and delete the generated folders.
